"I wash (myself).": "Saya mandi (membasuh diri).",
"Each other": "Saling",
"They know each other.": "Mereka saling kenal.",
"Always reflexive": "Selalu refleksif",
"I'm afraid. I laugh.": "Saya takut. Saya tertawa.",
"For yourself (si)": "Untuk diri sendiri (si)",
"I'll get a coffee.": "Saya pesan kopi.",
"Passive": "Pasif",
"Building is going on here.": "Di sini sedang ada pembangunan.",
"Impersonal": "Impersonal",
"How does one get there?": "Bagaimana cara ke sana?",
"Reflexive possessive svůj": "Kepemilikan refleksif svůj",
"svůj means 'one's own' and refers back to the subject of the clause. Use it instead of můj/tvůj/jeho when the owner is the subject.": "svůj berarti 'milik sendiri' dan merujuk ke subjek anak kalimat. Pakai ini sebagai ganti můj/tvůj/jeho jika pemiliknya adalah subjek.",
