"dvoje dveře (two doors)": "dvoje dveře (dua pintu)",
"troje kalhoty (three pairs of trousers)": "troje kalhoty (tiga celana)",
"Reported speech": "Kalimat tidak langsung",
"Czech keeps the original tense in reported speech. Questions use jestli/zda; commands use aby.": "Bahasa Ceko mempertahankan kala aslinya dalam kalimat tidak langsung. Pertanyaan memakai jestli/zda; perintah memakai aby.",
"She said she didn't have time.": "Dia bilang dia tidak punya waktu.",
"He asked where I lived.": "Dia bertanya di mana saya tinggal.",
"Keep the original tense: no shifting back like in English.": "Pertahankan kala aslinya: tidak ada pergeseran kala seperti dalam bahasa Inggris.",
"Past conditional": "Kondisional lampau",
"'Would have'. Formed with the conditional of být + l-participle. In speech, the present conditional is often used instead.": "'Seandainya sudah … tentu'. Dibentuk dengan kondisional být + partisip -l. Dalam percakapan, kondisional kini sering dipakai sebagai gantinya.",
"I would have called you.": "Saya tentu sudah meneleponmu.",
"I would have done": "saya tentu sudah melakukan",
"If I had known, I would have come.": "Seandainya saya tahu, saya tentu sudah datang.",
"Same, colloquial": "Sama, ragam sehari-hari",
"Passive voice": "Kalimat pasif",
"být + passive participle (agrees with subject). The agent goes in the instrumental. The reflexive passive with se is more common in everyday speech.": "být + partisip pasif (sesuai dengan subjek). Pelakunya memakai instrumental. Pasif refleksif dengan se lebih umum dalam percakapan sehari-hari.",
"The shop is closed.": "Tokonya tutup.",
"The contract was signed yesterday.": "Kontraknya ditandatangani kemarin.",
